{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1481346-how-to-block-a-summoning","id":1481346,"title":"How to Block a Summoning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-18T00:36:35-07:00","id":1481346,"title":"How to Block a Summoning?","content":"I may have screwed up in the campaign I'm running so I could do with some advice. The protagonists are Mages in the skinlands who have a group of murdered friends who became Wraiths.<br /> <br /> I've told the players that their friends cannot be summoned as they are somehow trapped in the Shadowlands by a Spectre (who has a group of buddies).<br /> <br /> However... I haven't worked out the detail of _how_ the Wraiths are blocked from being summoned, other than they they're trapped in some sort of mind game the Spectres are running in collusion with the Wraith's Shadows.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any suggestions for rules based means to block a summoning? It's a crossover game so anything from Mage, Wraith, or Vampire (20th anniversary editions) would work, or just any idea really?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T12:31:45-07:00","id":1481394,"title":"","content":"Could they have all been Harrowed in a group accident or ambush? If so, they're stuck in the Labyrinth until they get back, and perhaps the summoning cannot reach them there. After all, Wraith rules state that even Argos cannot get you out of a Harrowing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T14:24:24-07:00","id":1481405,"title":"","content":"A Harrowing was also the first thing that came to my mind since the OP mentioned they were somehow trapped in a mind game by spectres and their Shadows, and a Harrowing is similar. But there are other possibilities.<br /> <br /> The level 5 Argos ability Oubliette allows people to trap a wraith in the Tempest. Probably not the best solution for multiple wraiths over a long time.<br /> <br /> There could also easily be an Artifact that does the same. Each wraith could somehow be trapped in some kind of soul shackle that prevents them from being summoned. Chains for thralls are pretty ubiquitous in Wraith. While the description of Nhudri's Embrace does not mention it prevents being summoned, it makes perfect sense that they would. What person would want their Thralls disappearing whenever simply because they have one of the Quick who keeps summoning them?<br /> <br /> Lastly if there was something like a local Maelstrom hitting the Shadowlands where they are at, I also think it's justifiable for an ST to determine any summoning fails. It's the equivalent of a hurricane and could cancel out whatever force is trying to impel a wraith to appear.<br /> <br /> I also want to say that the Shadowlands are just one part of the Underworld. The Tempest, Byways, the islands that form the various Dark Kingdoms, the Far Shores, the Labyrinth, and the Void are all distinct parts of its geography. I don't know if the rules of summoning address the issue of where the wraith is actually located. In the original WoD: Sorcerer, it mentions in the Summoning Path that many dead souls are beyond contact - they are places the medium cannot reach. Now that could be just in terms of whether the wraith has transcended or fallen to Oblivion, but it seems reasonable to me that an ST could determine this also applies to wraiths who are in certain parts of the Underworld. Does it make sense that a Wraith visiting one of the Far Shores, trapped in the Labyrinth, or even in Stygia would be summonable - at least in the same way a wraith is in the Shadowlands? And in the Vampire Revised corebook under the Sepulchre Path of Necromancy it says many ghosts of the dead cannot be called - and some examples include &quot;unable to return to the mortal plane&quot; and &quot;lost in the eternal storm of the Underworld.&quot; Very similar to Sorcerer. At the very least you have justification to disallow any summoning if the wraiths simply aren't in the Shadowlands, but somewhere else in the Underworld. And if some spectre has trapped them somewhere, it could easily be in some place tucked away in the Tempest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-19-2022, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T15:27:52-07:00","id":1481562,"title":"","content":"On the Mage end:<br /> <br /> I would say for summoning a specific ghost with Magic(k) that's not relatively close one needs some Correspondence. More so if the ghost it's trapped and can't just travel by it's own means. (Spirit 2/Corr 2 for a long distance call. Spirit 2/Corr 3-4 to make them <i>appear </i>on your pressence chains or not).<br /> <br /> If they don't have the levels, that is that, but if they do: I still think this may be the weakest link on the summoning process. Because...<br /> <br /> *The Tempest itself would block a summoning, as Correspondence (and Time) does not work here. This is because the place it's constantly distorting space and time<br /> <br /> It's not so clear to me that this would prevent to reach into places that aren't the Tempest, but are <i>within </i>it, as Corresponence ignores the between - but one could rule that it does, that the time inside some Far Shores may be more stable but the Far Shore <i>itself</i>, as an island inside the Tempest, isn't so easy to reach from another place. Personaly I wouldn't make it impossible, but it could require more specialized magick or preparation.<br /> <br /> *As per the Book of Worlds a mage subject to a harrowing can't just escape it w/o solving it (Harrowing can happen trough Paradox, or dying while traveling as a disembodied soul). If a mage can't escape, it makes sense magick wouldn't be able to make others escape it either. All of the Labyrinth should similarly be hard to reach, I think.<br /> <br /> *Finally, if they have to be in the Shadowlands, you could similarly take the approach of &quot;too chaotic distortions of space to do a summon&quot; (combined with the ghosts inhability to just walk out of it) to tackle such shenanigans. Maybe the Spectres oppened a Nihil there and that's enough to make it prohibitively hard, if not impossible, to do the summon as long as they remain close to the door to the Tempest. Or maybe they have access to a similar power (Don't know what Spectres can do)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-20-2022, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T02:36:52-07:00","id":1481649,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, I'm going to go with Black Fox's suggestion of an artefact - a bangle or bracelet linked to a necklace, manufactured by a Spectre smith that makes the wearer of the bracelet want to stay in the presence of the necklace wearer (and also prevents summons) as that's good way of trapping the Wraiths in the Spectre's game without it being immediately obvious what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:09:10-07:00","id":1483630,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, Spirit 2 just gives a &quot;hello!&quot;, it doesnt force spirits to come. And using it to call a Wraith the other side of the world would take sometime for the Wraith to come over.<br /> <br /> If the Wraiths are in the Labyrinth, they might even hear the mages calling their names, but may be unable to do anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}